  "description": "<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://instructure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_73010000000000001/attachments/24286017/dp_app.css\"><p>Complete the problems here: <a class=\"instructure_file_link instructure_scribd_file inline_disabled\" title=\"HW 3.pdf\" href=\"https://instructure.charlotte.edu/courses/272933/files/34325465?verifier=904f0ddd-0d70-48a8-8c87-1ec44c0eec42&amp;wrap=1\" target=\"_blank\" data-canvas-previewable=\"false\" data-api-endpoint=\"https://instructure.charlotte.edu/api/v1/courses/272933/files/34325465\" data-api-returntype=\"File\">HW 3.pdf</a> and upload a pdf document of your work (note that we have restricted file types this time, but Canvas has a built in tool for pdfs if you need it). Please ensure that all problems are in a single document and that your work is legible.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br><strong>HW Guidelines:</strong><br>All work should be shown. <span style=\"color: #9e58bd;\"><em>No credit given for problems that show answers only</em></span>.&nbsp; If you use software/code (e.g. Matlab, python, Wolfram Alpha), that should be included. As much as possible, solve in terms of variables first, and then plug in numbers.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>All work should be your own. Cite any help or collaboration with peers, TAs, AI.&nbsp;<br><br>2 pts per problem</p>\n<p>Mostly graded on completion. -10% for incorrect answers (.1 per answer).&nbsp;</p><script src=\"https://instructure-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com/account_73010000000000001/attachments/24286016/dp_app.js\"></script>",
